{"id":"commission-outcomes","title":"Planning and Historic Preservation Commissions: approved, changed, refused or put off","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"What did the two commissions do with the items before them, and does that differ by kind of proposal, district or neighborhood?","finding":"The minutes (January 2019 to August 2022, with 1 earlier hearing in April 2018) record 1,226 decisions and 731 continuances (35.9% of actions): 28 decisions were disapprovals (2.3%) and 307 approvals with changes (25.0%). The share changed or disapproved runs from 17.5% (business: shop, restaurant, bar, cannabis, office, hotel, sign) to 46.7% (new housing, 1 to 9 homes, or an in-law unit) and by district from 17.2% (District 6; 22.0% expected from its mix of cases) to 42.9% (District 4; 40.2% expected); like for like, no district or neighborhood sits beyond what chance would produce.","how":"The minutes read are those of 208 hearings dated 2018-04-12 to 2022-08-17 (1 of them before 2019). One row per action block in the minutes. The action line is sorted by its words: “continued”; “withdrawn”; “disapproved”; “approved with conditions” exactly as proposed; approved “as amended”, “with modifications” or after taking discretionary review (counted as approved with changes); and plain approvals, adoptions and certifications. Informational items and the Zoning Administrator’s own variance rulings at joint hearings are left out. The kind of approval is the record type in the case number. Items at an address are placed by parcel, or by street address, under the 2012 district lines in force at the time; the “(District N)” the minutes print agrees with that placement in 94.5% of rows and prints 12 to 15 in 35 rows, which are not supervisor districts. “Expected” gives each decision the citywide rate of change or disapproval for its kind of approval and kind of proposal; a gap is called beyond chance at about the 1-in-100 level. Rates are printed only on 20 or more cases.","limits":"Outright refusal is rare: a weak proposal can be withdrawn or reshaped before a vote, and staff recommended approval in 1,857 of the 1,906 actions that print a recommendation. A continuance can be asked for by the applicant. The minutes obtainable cover January 2019 to August 2022, with 1 earlier hearing in April 2018 only; the minutes from August 2022 on are read in the screens of Planning hearings (planning_records). Districts differ sharply in what comes before the Commission, as the rows by kind of proposal show, so cases in two districts are often not like cases. A difference between areas, or between groups of cases, is not proof of bias. Areas differ in what is proposed, in zoning, lot sizes, building ages and land prices, and in who chooses to apply, object or appeal at all. ","columns":[{"k":"group","t":"Breakdown","type":"text"},{"k":"label","t":"Group","type":"text"},{"k":"actions","t":"Actions","type":"int"},{"k":"approved","t":"Approved as proposed","type":"int"},{"k":"conditions","t":"Approved, usual conditions","type":"int"},{"k":"changed","t":"Approved with changes","type":"int"},{"k":"disapproved","t":"Disapproved","type":"int"},{"k":"continued","t":"Continued","type":"int"},{"k":"withdrawn","t":"Withdrawn","type":"int"},{"k":"continuedShare","t":"Continued, share of actions","type":"pct"},{"k":"notAsProposedShare","t":"Changed or disapproved, share of decisions","type":"pct"},{"k":"expected","t":"Expected from its mix of cases","type":"pct"},{"k":"beyondChance","t":"Gap beyond chance?","type":"text"},{"k":"disapprovedShare","t":"Disapproved, share of decisions","type":"pct"}],"rows":[{"group":"All actions","label":"Both commissions","actions":2037,"approved":443,"conditions":448,"changed":307,"disapproved":28,"continued":731,"withdrawn":80,"continuedShare":0.3589,"notAsProposedShare":0.2732,"disapprovedShare":0.0228,"expected":null,"beyondChance":""},{"group":"By body","label":"Planning Commission","actions":1672,"approved":203,"conditions":406,"changed":